  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39835972",
      "title": "Styling React Apps with Vanilla CSS - Pros & Cons",
      "sourceHash": "1bfd1b1db9eaa4b83f9d557b6b0b55a140b23604f70db07762d537f9304067b3",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.42,
          "end": 2.4,
          "en": "So, as shown in the last lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.4,
          "end": 4.98,
          "en": "you can use Vanilla CSS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.98,
          "end": 9,
          "en": "by simply adding CSS rules in CSS files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9,
          "end": 13.173,
          "en": "and importing those CSS files into your JSX files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.31,
          "end": 16.95,
          "en": "That all works and is really great",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.95,
          "end": 20.31,
          "en": "if you want to work with Vanilla CSS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.31,
          "end": 22.62,
          "en": "or if you've got another developer or designer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.62,
          "end": 25.68,
          "en": "who's working on those CSS files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.68,
          "end": 29.64,
          "en": "because that person can just deliver these files to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.64,
          "end": 32.64,
          "en": "You just import them, and therefore you can work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.64,
          "end": 35.07,
          "en": "on the components and the JSX code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.07,
          "end": 38.64,
          "en": "and the other person can work on the CSS code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.64,
          "end": 42.63,
          "en": "That's one advantage of using this Vanilla CSS approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.63,
          "end": 45.93,
          "en": "And of course, you can simply write CSS code as you know it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.93,
          "end": 49.41,
          "en": "and you don't have to follow any special conventions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.41,
          "end": 53.25,
          "en": "because it is just Vanilla CSS code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.25,
          "end": 57.18,
          "en": "Therefore, when it comes to using Vanilla CSS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.18,
          "end": 60.66,
          "en": "for styling React apps, one advantage is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.66,
          "end": 64.5,
          "en": "that you get your CSS code out of the JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.5,
          "end": 68.19,
          "en": "and you will soon see that this is not necessarily the case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.19,
          "end": 71.61,
          "en": "for all available styling options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.61,
          "end": 76.32,
          "en": "Another advantage is that you do write Vanilla CSS code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.32,
          "end": 80.82,
          "en": "So, CSS as you know, and maybe love it or maybe hate it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 80.82,
          "end": 81.813,
          "en": "Depends on you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.89,
          "end": 85.35,
          "en": "And of course, another advantage related",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 85.35,
          "end": 90.35,
          "en": "to that decoupling from JSX code is that different people",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 90.53999999999999,
          "end": 94.62,
          "en": "can work on that code so that you can work on a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 94.62,
          "end": 97.71000000000001,
          "en": "without getting distracted or interrupted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 97.71000000000001,
          "end": 100.263,
          "en": "by the person who needs to add some styling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 102.03,
          "end": 104.13,
          "en": "Of course, we also got some disadvantages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 104.13,
          "end": 106.53,
          "en": "with Vanilla CSS though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 106.53,
          "end": 110.055,
          "en": "For example, you need to know CSS in order to write it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 110.055,
          "end": 112.62299999999999,
          "en": "unless you have a colleague who does that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 113.85,
          "end": 115.402,
          "en": "And then, there's another",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.402,
          "end": 119.03999999999999,
          "en": "which we'll take a closer look in the next lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 119.03999999999999,
          "end": 122.43,
          "en": "Because when writing Vanilla CSS code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 122.43,
          "end": 124.77,
          "en": "when using the solution I just showed you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 124.77,
          "end": 129.77,
          "en": "in the last lecture, then that code and those CSS rules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 130.14,
          "end": 133.32,
          "en": "are not scoped to components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 133.32,
          "end": 136.56,
          "en": "which means you can have styling clashes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 136.56,
          "end": 138.75,
          "en": "between different components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 138.75,
          "end": 143.61,
          "en": "if you are using CSS rules that may affect JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 143.61,
          "end": 145.92000000000002,
          "en": "stored in different components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 145.92000000000002,
          "end": 147.39,
          "en": "But we'll take a closer look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 147.39,
          "end": 150.633,
          "en": "at that disadvantage in the next lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
